# Competency question: "What is the signature — the operand number system and the
# result number system — of each arithmetic operator?"  This exercises the rule that
# every math:ArithmeticOperation carries its signature over the number-system tower
# through math:operatorDomain and math:operatorCodomain (both mandatory on the class,
# so a strict BGP). Over the module the answer is the eight operators: the field
# operators Addition/Subtraction/Multiplication/Division and Exponentiation over
# ℝ → ℝ, Root and Logarithm over ℝ → ℂ (their real inputs can land in ℂ), and the
# unary Negation over the signed extended real line ℝ̄ → ℝ̄ (it carries the poles).
PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>

SELECT ?operator ?operatorDomain ?operatorCodomain WHERE {
    ?operator a math:ArithmeticOperation ;
              math:operatorDomain ?operatorDomain ;
              math:operatorCodomain ?operatorCodomain .
}
ORDER BY ?operator
